      "id": 1,
      "text": "Valley Mills was named after a flour mill built on the Bosque River in 1867 by a local doctor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Mills%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Gulf, Colorado and Santa Fe Railway laid tracks a mile south of town in 1881, Valley Mills moved across the Bosque River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historictexas.net/city/valley-mills-texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Valley Mills earned its status as a Recorded Texas Historic Landmark in 1973.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
